                    ; object on the right -- `1 instanceof Math` -- is a
                    ; TypeError too. Built-in constructor NAMES are function
                    ; values now, so they pass this on their own.
                    if (irKind == "Identifier") {
                        ; A function whose `prototype` is not an object is a
                        ; TypeError as well, which the chain walk below reports
                        ; -- but only if it is reached, so a binding holding a
                        ; function is left alone here.
